## Why Each Piece Was Built

| Component | Why |
|---|---|
| **Docker Compose** | One command to start all infrastructure. No manual PostgreSQL/Redis installation. Reproducible across machines. |
| **Prisma ORM** | Type-safe database queries. Schema changes generate migrations automatically. TypeScript knows the exact shape of every query result. |
| **Environment validation** | App crashes on startup with a clear message if config is wrong — not 10 minutes later with a cryptic error deep in a handler. |
| **Singleton clients** | One database connection pool, one Redis connection. Multiple instances would exhaust connection limits. |
| **Structured logging (Pino)** | JSON logs can be searched and filtered in production. `console.log` cannot. |
| **Custom ApiError** | Consistent error responses. Factory methods (`ApiError.notFound()`) make error creation clean. |
| **asyncHandler** | Express 4 silently swallows async errors. This wrapper catches them and forwards to the error handler. |
| **Centralized error handler** | One place to format all errors. Routes just throw; they don't construct responses. |
| **Zod validation middleware** | Express doesn't validate request bodies. Zod catches invalid input before it reaches business logic. |

