## Trade-offs

| Decision | Alternative | Why We Chose This |
|---|---|---|
| Prisma ORM | Raw SQL / Knex | Prisma gives type-safe queries and auto-generated migrations. Trade-off: less flexible for complex SQL. Acceptable for this project. |
| Pino logger | Winston / console.log | Pino is the fastest Node.js logger. Winston is more feature-rich but slower. Pino is sufficient. |
| Express 4 | Express 5 / Fastify | Express 4 is the most widely used, most documented, and most interview-relevant. Express 5 has native async support but is still newer. |
| Zod validation | Joi / class-validator | Zod has first-class TypeScript support — schemas automatically produce types. Joi requires separate type definitions. |
| UUID primary keys | Auto-increment integers | UUIDs are globally unique — safe in distributed systems. Auto-increment leaks information (competitor can guess your user count). Trade-off: UUIDs are larger (16 bytes vs 4 bytes). |

